    "title": "Dr. Chef Basu’s Monarch Giant Celeriac Stem Velouté & Silky Emulsion",
    "category": "Soups & Veloutés",
    "prepTime": "15 min",
    "cookTime": "30 min",
    "yieldAmount": "1.2 Liters (6 portions)",
    "mainByproduct": "Monarch Giant Celeriac Trimmings & Byproducts",
    "image": "/assets/ingredients/celeriac.jpg",
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "amount": "500g",
        "item": "Washed, peeled monarch giant celeriac stems, stalks & core trimmings"
      },
      {
        "amount": "60g",
        "item": "Shallots or scallion whites, finely sliced"
      },
      {
        "amount": "500ml",
        "item": "Light vegetable scrap court bouillon"
      },
      {
        "amount": "60g",
        "item": "Cultured grass-fed unsalted butter (cubed cold)"
      },
      {
        "amount": "4 sprigs",
        "item": "Fresh garden thyme and flat-leaf parsley stems"
      }
    ],
    "method": [
      "1. Sweat Aromatics: Melt 15g butter in a heavy saucepan over medium-low heat. Sweat shallots and thyme sprigs for 4 minutes without browning.",
      "2. Mirepoix Addition: Mandoline monarch giant celeriac stems to 3mm uniform thickness and add to pan. Season with 6g kosher salt to draw moisture.",
      "3. Simmer: Pour in warm vegetable court bouillon. Bring to a gentle sub-boil (92°C) and simmer covered for 18 minutes until tender to knife tip.",
      "4. Cold Butter Emulsion: Transfer to a commercial blender. Discard woody thyme stems. Emulsify at maximum RPM while dropping in remaining cold butter cubes one by one.",
      "5. Chinois Pass: Pass through a fine conical chinois. Adjust seasoning with a squeeze of fresh lemon juice. Garnish with herb stem oil."
    ],
    "chefTips": "Dr. Chef Supritam Basu's Master Tip: The Pectin Methyl Esterase (PME) present in brassica and vegetable stems softens beautifully around 85°C. Blitzing cold butter into hot vegetable purees creates a stable micellar emulsion that needs zero heavy cream.",
