    "chefTips": "Dr. Chef Supritam Basu's Master Tip: Pangrattato is historically known as 'poor man's parmesan' in Southern Italy. When made with high-hydration sourdough and good olive oil, its crunch elevates any fresh pasta dish far above grated cheese.",
