    "id": "recipe-420-clarified-butter-toasted-milk-solids",
    "title": "Dr. Chef Basu’s Clarified Butter Toasted Milk Solids Whey Dulce de Leche Caramel",
    "category": "Pastry & Confections",
    "prepTime": "10 min",
    "cookTime": "1h 30m Slow Simmer",
    "yieldAmount": "400g Spreadable Caramel",
    "mainByproduct": "Clarified Butter Toasted Milk Solids Trimmings & Byproducts",
    "image": "/assets/ingredients/milk_whey.jpg",
    "ingredients": [
      {
        "amount": "1000ml",
        "item": "Sweet culinary clarified butter toasted milk solids whey liquid"
      },
      {
        "amount": "250ml",
        "item": "Fresh whole cream"
      },
      {
        "amount": "200g",
        "item": "Turbinado raw cane sugar"
      },
      {
        "amount": "3g",
        "item": "Flaky Maldon sea salt"
      },
      {
        "amount": "1/2 tsp",
        "item": "Baking soda (sodium bicarbonate)"
      }
    ],
    "method": [
      "1. Pan Setup: Combine whey, whole cream, and sugar in a wide, heavy-bottomed copper or stainless saucier.",
      "2. Alkaline Shift: Whisk in 1/2 tsp baking soda; this raises pH to 7.2, accelerating the Maillard browning reaction tenfold.",
      "3. Simmer: Bring to a simmer over medium heat, stirring with a heat-resistant silicone spatula to prevent scorching on the pan base.",
      "4. Caramelization: As water evaporates over 75 minutes, the natural milk sugars (lactose) and proteins caramelize into a deep bronze spread.",
      "5. Finishing: Fold in flaky Maldon sea salt off the heat. Pour into clean jars. Outstanding with artisan ice creams and tarts."
    ],
    "chefTips": "Dr. Chef Supritam Basu's Master Tip: The traditional Norwegian brown cheese Gjetost is made exactly this way. The high lactose content in whey creates a caramel that has naturally lower glycemic impact and richer savory complexity than cane sugar caramel.",
